comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T12:40:38.715Z",codex-sol,"Main history contains no coverage repair after the reported failures. Capturing branch-level LCOV from the existing focused diff consumers on Node 22, then adding deterministic cases before changing implementation. Local work runs targeted tests, lint and typecheck; the full unchanged release gates run in CI as requested."
  "2026-11-06T12:51:58.275Z",codex-sol,"Focused existing diff consumers passed on unchanged main source with the pinned SDK: Node 22 and Node 26 each report 100 percent lines/branches/functions over diff.ts. Both LCOV reports contain 146 branches. The reported failure implies 146 of 147 branches; investigating the additional range with a broader reproduction rather than weakening thresholds. Latest main release CI has successful Node 22 and 26 jobs but failed simulation-release-gates, so those green legs do not close the issue."
  "2026-11-06T13:01:07.505Z",codex-sol,"Root cause established from real V8 data: merging 17 process captures in a deterministic shuffled order reproduces 147 branches with exactly one zero range, the nullish fallback in planInput.seeds (declaredSeeds ?? []). The earlier Array.isArray guard rejects every selected nullish inventory, making that fallback unexecutable. Other merge orders omit that range and show 146/146. A failing-first real-process SDK regression now reports the uncovered range as ?? []; it exercises both selection orders, explicit empty arrays, missing/null/object/string refusals, and audited managed enrollment on nongit trackers. Removing only the redundant fallback preserves every supported behavior and threshold. Stopped the broader local reproduction after capturing this cause; final full gates belong to CI as requested."
  "2026-11-06T13:02:36.646Z",codex-sol,"Behavioral revert proof: restoring only the old selected-inventory fallback in a disposable source copy makes tests/diff-coverage.test.ts fail with the zero-count range ?? []; restoring the fixed expression passes. No guard, accepted value, runtime behavior, percentage threshold or source exclusion changed. The focused real-process regression is deterministic independently of native report merge order."
  "2026-11-06T13:06:51.941Z",codex-sol,"Fixed-source Node 22 targeted coverage passes 79/79 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations, with 100 percent lines, branches and functions for diff.ts under unchanged 100 percent thresholds. Node 26 combined real-process diff/closeout regressions pass 11/11. The exact one-expression revert fails the counter assertion and restoration passes. Lint, typecheck, test compilation, build, complete docstrings and isolated-home strict tracker health pass. Default-home health correctly reports a global extension/host version skew; isolated CI-style state has no finding. Full Node 22/26 and npm/Bun gates plus bot review remain pending in PR CI. Releasing the implementation claim for external verification; item remains in_progress."
